<Layout title="Movie games like Wordle · Daily film puzzles to try" description="Looking for movie games like Wordle or games like Framed? Compare daily film puzzles and try Reelillion, where rare movie answers earn more points.">
  <article class="content-page"><p class="eyebrow">Same daily habit. Different obsession.</p><h1 class="page-title">For the film lover<br />in your group chat.</h1><p class="lede">If the best part of Wordle is comparing a tiny daily result with your friends, a movie puzzle might be your next ritual.</p>
    <section class="prose"><p>“Movie Wordle” can mean several different things. Some games reveal one hidden film. Others ask you to connect credits or name a title that fits a category. Here are a few ways to choose.</p>
    <h2>Want to guess one movie? Try Framed.</h2><p><a href="https://framed.wtf/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Framed</a> is built around identifying a film from images. Classic mode provides up to six frames, making it an easy pick if you want a daily mystery with a clear answer. Its One Frame mode offers a tighter visual challenge.</p>
    <h2>Prefer a grid of possibilities? Try MovieGrid.</h2><p><a href="https://moviegrid.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">MovieGrid</a> asks for films at the intersection of different criteria. You draw on your knowledge of actors, genres, years and other details rather than recognize a single image. Several titles may fit a cell.</p>
    <h2>Want to name your own answer? Try Reelillion.</h2><p>Our game asks seven “Name a movie…” questions. Any film in the catalog that satisfies the prompt can work, and less common answers earn more points. It's a short daily test of recall with a spoiler-free share card at the end.</p><p>There are no letters to reveal and no single secret title to chase. Instead, you decide whether to play a familiar favorite or reach further into your movie memory. Read the <a href="/how-to-play/">full rules</a> before your first screening.</p>
    <h2>If you're looking for games like Framed</h2><p>Pick another visual guessing game if you love recognizing cinematography. Pick a grid game if cast and credits are your strength. Pick Reelillion if you want a reason to bring up the little-known film you keep recommending to everyone.</p>
    <h2>Can you play with friends?</h2><p>Reelillion's Daily gives everyone the same seven prompts. Share your finished score or send a challenge link so a friend can try the same date. Share cards contain points and tier emojis, without revealing film titles.</p>
    <h2>Do you need an account?</h2><p>Reelillion's Daily and general practice sessions work without an account. Your device identifier and streak stay associated with this browser; changing browsers or clearing site storage can break that continuity.</p><p>We make Reelillion and are not affiliated with Wordle, Framed or MovieGrid. Features on other sites can change; the links above go directly to their creators' sites.</p></section>
